# Phase 12 / Step 2 — LACN OOD threshold recalibration

OOD cohort: PAD-UFES-20, N = 200
Prevalence: 50.0% malignant

## Step 1 — Otsu mask reliability
  Reliable masks: 172/200 (86.0%)
  Mean area fraction: 0.379

Target Lab mean (Phase 9 ref): [155.44000244140625, 142.80999755859375, 135.4600067138672]

## Step 2 — LACN applied
  LACN applied (reliable mask): 172/200
  Mean dP_LACN (LACN - original P): +0.0437

## Step 3 — Stratified split (seed=42)
  Calibration: N=100 (pos=50, neg=50)
  Test:        N=100 (pos=50, neg=50)

## Step 4 — Threshold recalibration on calibration set
  Target recall: 0.79
  Smallest tau achieving recall >= 0.79: tau_LACN=0.670 (cal recall=0.820, cal spec=0.620).

## Step 5 — Test-set evaluation (N=100)
  AUC (no LACN): 0.8500
  AUC (LACN):    0.7984

  (A) No LACN  + tau=0.661  : recall=0.820  spec=0.720  prec=0.745  f1=0.781  TP=41 FN=9 TN=36 FP=14
  (B) LACN     + tau=0.661  : recall=0.860  spec=0.600  prec=0.683  f1=0.761  TP=43 FN=7 TN=30 FP=20
  (C) LACN     + tau_LACN   : recall=0.840  spec=0.640  prec=0.700  f1=0.764  TP=42 FN=8 TN=32 FP=18

## Verdict
  Recall    : A=0.820 -> C=0.840  (delta +0.020)
  Specificity: A=0.720 -> C=0.640    (delta -0.080)
  F1        : A=0.781 -> C=0.764       (delta -0.017)
  -> LACN recalibrated preserves recall but loses specificity. Partial win.

